<Base title="About" description="Background, career and interests of Luke Charbonneau, a software engineer in Boulder, Colorado.">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="page-header">
      <h1>About</h1>
      <p>Physicist turned software engineer, based in Boulder, Colorado.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose section">
      <p>
        I graduated from the University of Colorado in 2016 with both a B.A. and an M.S. in Physics. My graduate research was in experimental ultrafast optics, which deals with pulses of light that are extremely short in time (less than 10<sup>-12</sup> seconds). You can read more about it on my <a href="/research/">research page</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        After graduating, I worked in the optics industry, first as a measurement engineer at Photon Kinetics and then as Head of Product Development at <a href="https://crunchtec.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Crunch Technologies</a> in Boulder, designing and building software used by optics production facilities and research institutions. Once I decided to focus on software, my background as an optical hardware developer and researcher helped me build user-friendly tools for labs around the world.
      </p>
      <p>
        Today I build and maintain data processing pipelines for NASA missions at the Laboratory for Atmospheric and Space Physics (<a href="https://lasp.colorado.edu/" rel="noopener noreferrer">LASP</a>). My primary mission is the Total and Spectral Solar Irradiance Sensor (<a href="https://lasp.colorado.edu/tsis/" rel="noopener noreferrer">TSIS-1</a>), a pair of instruments mounted on the International Space Station that measure the Sun’s output every day. Engineers at LASP, including me, process and correct those measurements into scientific data products that give climate researchers critical insight into the Sun’s influence on Earth’s systems.
      </p>
      <p>
        I also offer freelance software development through Castle Scientific LLC, registered in Colorado.
      </p>

      <h2>Outside of work</h2>
      <p>
        I spend a lot of time outdoors hiking, skiing and backpacking. I also play piano and read a lot of history; my favorite topics right now are the late Roman Republic and the Cold War.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
